Vendored from FlashAttention (https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention), `hopper/` at commit
3451a2a67a24eeed8af54d3c5b8d219577113797 (2026-10-04), BSD-3-Clause (see LICENSE). Upstream
builds it against CUTLASS 7127592; here it compiles against the CUTLASS the engine already
fetches (v4.6.1).

What is here, and why: FlashAttention-3's sm90 forward kernel (wgmma, TMA for Q/O, warp
specialisation, intra-warpgroup softmax overlap) and the varlen scheduler's prepare kernel, so the
serving engine's prompt attention on H100/H200 runs the kernel vLLM runs there
(`src/serve/ops/gqa_sm90/gqa_fa3_hdim*.cu` instantiate one configuration per head dim, 64, 128
and 256, cache dtype, BF16 or e4m3, and mask, causal or a causal sliding window). Only the forward
headers are taken, plus the split-KV combine (`flash_fwd_combine_kernel.h`,
`flash_fwd_combine_launch_template.h`), which merges the partial outputs of the split forward the
decode route runs (`src/serve/ops/gqa_sm90/gqa_fa3_*_split.cu`, `gqa_fa3_combine.cu`); the
Python/PyTorch API (`flash_api.cpp`, whose split heuristic `gqa_fa3.cu` follows), the backward and
the generated instantiation files are not.

Local change: `cuda_check.h` throws `std::runtime_error` where upstream prints and calls
`exit(1)`, so a failed launch surfaces as an engine error instead of ending the server.
